## How to complain

Email **hello@juniperhealth.info** with "Complaint" in the subject line. Please tell us:

- your name and how to contact you
- what went wrong, and when
- the page or pages involved, if relevant
- what you would like us to do to put it right

If you need to complain in a different way, for example because of a disability, tell us and we will help.

## What happens next

1. **We acknowledge your complaint** within **5 working days**.
2. **We look into it** fairly and carefully.
3. **We reply in full** within **20 working days**. If we need longer, we will tell you why and when you can expect an answer.

## Complaints about your personal information

If your complaint is about how we have used your personal information, the **Data (Use and Access) Act 2025** gives you the right to complain to us first. We will acknowledge it within 30 days at most, deal with it without unnecessary delay, and tell you the outcome.

If you are not happy with our response, you can complain to the **Information Commissioner's Office (ICO)**:

- Website: ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint
- Helpline: 0303 123 1113

## Complaints we cannot deal with

We are not part of the DWP or the NHS, so we cannot change a benefit decision or deal with complaints about them.

- **To challenge a benefit decision,** see [how to challenge a PIP decision](/benefits/pip/challenge-a-decision/). The same steps apply to Attendance Allowance and DLA.
- **To complain about the DWP,** follow the complaints process on GOV.UK.
- **To complain about something you bought through an affiliate link,** contact the shop, as it sold you the item.

